                <h2 id="faqs">FAQs — Credit Utilization 30% Rule</h2>
                <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 not-prose">
                    <div class="rounded-xl border p-4 bg-white"><div class="font-bold text-[14px]">Is 30% utilization bad?</div><p class="mt-1 text-[13px] leading-6 text-slate-600">Not terrible, but it's the borderline. Under 30% keeps you out of high-risk. Under 10% is excellent and helps fastest if you're building from 0 or 550.</p></div>
                    <div class="rounded-xl border p-4 bg-white"><div class="font-bold text-[14px]">Does paying in full help utilization?</div><p class="mt-1 text-[13px] leading-6 text-slate-600">Only if you pay BEFORE statement reports. Paying in full after statement still shows the balance that printed on the statement. Pay early to show low utilization.</p></div>
                    <div class="rounded-xl border p-4 bg-white"><div class="font-bold text-[14px]">What if I have $300 limit — what should I spend?</div><p class="mt-1 text-[13px] leading-6 text-slate-600">Spend what you need, but make statement report $9-$27 (3-9%). Easiest: use card for gas or Netflix, set autopay mid-cycle, leave $10.</p></div>
                    <div class="rounded-xl border p-4 bg-white"><div class="font-bold text-[14px]">Is 0% utilization good for credit?</div><p class="mt-1 text-[13px] leading-6 text-slate-600">It's okay, but slightly less optimal than 1-3% showing active use. FICO likes seeing responsible use. Don't overthink — 0% won't hurt long term.</p></div>
                    <div class="rounded-xl border p-4 bg-white"><div class="font-bold text-[14px]">How long does high utilization hurt?</div><p class="mt-1 text-[13px] leading-6 text-slate-600">Only one reporting cycle in current models. Lower it this month, your score can rebound next month when new low balance is reported to bureaus.</p></div>
                </div>

